course: dictionary
lesson: 11356
title: Zone: an area with its own purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A zone is an area of a place that is different from the areas around it, or one used for a special purpose. «A no-parking zone» is where you must not park, and «a school zone» is where cars must drive slowly. The words before zone tell you what the area is for.
explain: Look for clue words around zone. «Time zones» in a sentence about flying tells you the topic is clocks. «Going east, the clock usually moves one hour later in each new time zone» shows that a time zone is an area where all the clocks show the same time.
explain: Zone can also be a verb. «To zone out» means to stop paying attention. If Maya zoned out during a spelling test, the context tells you she stopped listening, not that she left the room.
fact: A zone is an area that is different from the areas around it, or one used for a special purpose.
fact: «A no-parking zone» and «a school zone» are zones you see in everyday life.
fact: A time zone is an area of the world that uses the same clock time.
fact: «Going east, the clock usually moves one hour later in each new time zone.»
fact: To zone out means to stop paying attention.
exercise: «Going east, the clock usually moves one hour later in each new time zone.» What is a time zone? | A sea mile from the coast | *An area of the world that uses the same clock time | A zone where cars must drive slowly | A kind of watch that runs fast
exercise: «A school zone» is a place where cars must drive slowly. What does zone mean here? | A loud noise made by cars | A part of the sea far from land | *An area of a place used for a special purpose | A kind of school bus
exercise: Maya says, «I zoned out during the spelling test.» What does zoned out mean? | *Stopped paying attention | Got very cross | Went out to play | Finished first
test: «Spanish scientists reported that eastern tree frogs in the zone are darker than usual.» In this sentence, zone means | A clock that runs slow | A kind of frog | *An area that is different from the areas around it | A sea mile from the coast
test: «The library has a quiet zone where talking is not allowed.» What is the quiet zone? | A cosy chair for reading aloud | A shelf full of loud books | *An area of the library used for a special purpose, where talking is not allowed | A window that opens onto the playground
exam: «An exclusive economic zone reaches up to 200 nautical miles out to sea.» What is a nautical mile? | *A sea mile, a bit under 2 kilometres | A map of the coast | A fast boat | A mile on land
